{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1447969-reptilians-and-dinosaurs","id":1447969,"title":"Reptilians and Dinosaurs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-08T13:07:51-07:00","id":1447969,"title":"Reptilians and Dinosaurs","content":"In <b>Adventure!</b> preview there is mention of Dinosaurs in Strange Places. I want to make story about 'Lizardman' and Dinosaurs exactly. <b>Are there some stats for Trinity / Storypath for those two groups?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T13:18:46-07:00","id":1447973,"title":"","content":"In Adventure there are stats for Raptors and in Aberrant there are stats for a cloned Tyrannosaur.<br /> <br /> You may need to build reptilians, but honestly just make them humans with the kinds of power/tech you need, and green and commanding the largest companies in the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T19:18:14-07:00","id":1448008,"title":"","content":"The Adventure! companion book will include a section (Strange New Life) with rules for creating non-human characters &quot;from intelligent apes to living robots&quot;. Doesn't specifically mention Lizard Men but they are a staple of the adventure pulp genre so it's likely to have something usable for that purpose if not explicit Lizard man stats.<br /> <br /> But that is still a ways off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T20:10:18-07:00","id":1448012,"title":"","content":"I'd suggest that you find stats for an alligator or crocodile (some Onyx Path or White Wolf book had to have those). Then create a human with a crocodilian's armor and sensory abilities. Also it's other abilities like hibernation and diving abilities.<br /> <br /> Your pastiche should work well enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T09:38:17-07:00","id":1448996,"title":"","content":"From the KAIS institute Velociraptor robot, it <a href=\"https://singularityhub.com/2014/06/13/velociraptor-robot-can-run-down-a-human-luckily-it-lacks-claws/\" target=\"_blank\">seems that Raptors would be twice faster than average athlete</a> - and slightly faster than fastest man alive, Usain Bolt- <b>Would it mean Raptors should have Speed Scale against humans? </b><br /> <br /> 'In a recently released video, KAIST shows Raptor running the treadmill at a leg-blurring top speed of 46 kph (28.5 mph). That\u2019s faster than the fastest human sprinter (Usain Bolt), and matches Boston Dynamics\u2019 fleet-footed robot Cheetah. (Raptor has <a href=\"http://spectrum.ieee.org/automaton/robotics/robotics-hardware/fast-running-biped-robot-based-on-velociraptor\" target=\"_blank\">momentarily achieved</a> even higher speeds of 48 kph, or 29.8 mph.)'<br /> <br /> Typical human athletes data - <a href=\"https://trackspikes.co.uk/average-sprinting-speed/\" target=\"_blank\">https://trackspikes.co.uk/average-sprinting-speed/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T12:53:33-07:00","id":1449032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1447969-reptilians-and-dinosaurs?p=1448996#post1448996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the KAIS institute Velociraptor robot, it <a href=\"https://singularityhub.com/2014/06/13/velociraptor-robot-can-run-down-a-human-luckily-it-lacks-claws/\" target=\"_blank\">seems that Raptors would be twice faster than average athlete</a> - and slightly faster than fastest man alive, Usain Bolt- <b>Would it mean Raptors should have Speed Scale against humans? </b><br /> <br /> 'In a recently released video, KAIST shows Raptor running the treadmill at a leg-blurring top speed of 46 kph (28.5 mph). That\u2019s faster than the fastest human sprinter (Usain Bolt), and matches Boston Dynamics\u2019 fleet-footed robot Cheetah. (Raptor has <a href=\"http://spectrum.ieee.org/automaton/robotics/robotics-hardware/fast-running-biped-robot-based-on-velociraptor\" target=\"_blank\">momentarily achieved</a> even higher speeds of 48 kph, or 29.8 mph.)'<br /> <br /> Typical human athletes data - <a href=\"https://trackspikes.co.uk/average-sprinting-speed/\" target=\"_blank\">https://trackspikes.co.uk/average-sprinting-speed/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The stats hardly show any scale, so you need to put them in place. In the case, Raptors are scale 2 in speed and Tyrannosaurs are scale 3 in size (a car would be scale 2, and a house scale 3, that is basically how big a Tyrannosaur is).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T13:10:07-07:00","id":1449037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (a car would be scale 2, and a house scale 3, that is basically how big a Tyrannosaur is). </div> </div> </div>I made T-Rex too small, compared to PCs on map? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> 