\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24985\" data-vbnamecard=\"24985\">Mateus Luz</a>?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Silurians / Reptilians / Lizard Man / Homo Reptilia / Reptilia Sapiens</b></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/t8FC32a.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/t8FC32a.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The first Silurians are prehistoric and scientifically advanced sentient humanoids who predate the dawn of man; in their backstory, the Silurians went into self-induced hibernation to survive what they predicted to be a large atmospheric upheaval caused by the Earth capturing the Moon. Now they crawling out of their millenia long sleep.<br /> Some of Silurinas did not gone to hibernate \u2013 but they become savage after centuries outside of their former empire civilization. Here are stats for those \u2018barbarians\u2019 Reptialians, focused on hunting and survival.<br /> <br /> <b>Archetype:</b> Professional \\ Foe<br /> <b>Qualities: </b>Natural Weapon ( Claws ), Soft Armor 1 ( Light Armors ), Subterranean Movement, Sure Footed, Unnatural Behavior ( Hunting )<br /> <b>Flairs: </b>Seeing Red, Here I Come<br /> <b>Drive:</b> Hunt and survive<br /> <b>Weakness: Cold Blooded</b> \u2013 As reptiles, Reptilia Sapiens are becoming more and more sluggish as colder it becomes. They got -1 to any action for each 10 degrees under room temperature. Assuming typical room temperature is circa 20 Celsius Degrees, so on 0 Degrees they would have -2 to actions \u2013 and -4 at -20 Degrees outside, <b><i>on top </i></b>of normal modifiers for other characters.<br /> <b>Primary Pool (7):</b> Hunting, Tracking, Close Combat<br /> <b>Secondary Pool (5):</b> ???<br /> <b>Desperation Pool:</b> 3<br /> <b>Health:</b> 2<br /> <b>Defense</b>: 1 ( Soft Armor 1 )<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 4<br /> <b>Extras:</b> +1 Enhancement to Hunting and Close Combat<br /> <b>Attacks:</b><br /> <b><i>Claws </i></b>- Enhancement 1, Natural, Range: Close, Lethal, Messy, Piercing<br /> <b><i>Spear - </i></b> Enhancement 1, Range: Close, Lethal, Piercing<br /> <b><i>Sword -</i></b> Enhancement 1, Range: Close, Lethal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-21-2021, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-21T13:06:29-07:00","id":1449207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1447969-reptilians-and-dinosaurs?p=1448996#post1448996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the KAIS institute Velociraptor robot, it <a href=\"https://singularityhub.com/2014/06/13/velociraptor-robot-can-run-down-a-human-luckily-it-lacks-claws/\" target=\"_blank\">seems that Raptors would be twice faster than average athlete</a> - and slightly faster than fastest man alive, Usain Bolt- <b>Would it mean Raptors should have Speed Scale against humans? </b><br /> <br /> 'In a recently released video, KAIST shows Raptor running the treadmill at a leg-blurring top speed of 46 kph (28.5 mph). That\u2019s faster than the fastest human sprinter (Usain Bolt), and matches Boston Dynamics\u2019 fleet-footed robot Cheetah. (Raptor has <a href=\"http://spectrum.ieee.org/automaton/robotics/robotics-hardware/fast-running-biped-robot-based-on-velociraptor\" target=\"_blank\">momentarily achieved</a> even higher speeds of 48 kph, or 29.8 mph.)'<br /> <br /> Typical human athletes data - <a href=\"https://trackspikes.co.uk/average-sprinting-speed/\" target=\"_blank\">https://trackspikes.co.uk/average-sprinting-speed/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>That robot might not be running in a way that the dinosaur in question could. Muscles from the pubic process would have anchored the upper legs a lot more than you see in mammals, making them stiff in order to gain stability. Any running would have been from the knee, which would have made for a much slower chase, if any. It might have been that they didn't pursue prey overly much, but rather fall on it after climbing trees, landing toe-first and driving the lengthy &quot;toe claw&quot; in with gravity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-21T19:08:27-07:00","id":1449223,"title":"","content":"I like the way you made them and the idea of cold blooded that slow down in cold weather is interesting.<br /> <br /> While I like the more precise (from this to that) temperature, my suggestion is a more open ended definition. On \u201croom temperature\u201d they gain no restrictions, on cold temperatures they gain a condition that causes a +1 difficulty on all physical actions and on extremely cold temperatures +2 on difficulties of all physical and +1 on all other actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-21T20:31:03-07:00","id":1449224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1447969-reptilians-and-dinosaurs?p=1449200#post1449200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Weakness: Cold Blooded</b> \u2013 As reptiles, Reptilia Sapiens are becoming more and more sluggish as colder it becomes. They got -1 to any action for each 10 degrees under room temperature. Assuming typical room temperature is circa 20 Celsius Degrees, so on 0 Degrees they would have -2 to actions \u2013 and -4 at -20 Degrees outside, <b><i>on top </i></b>of normal modifiers for other characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a really wordy way to just say -1 per 10 degrees below 20 Celsius. <br /> <br /> And as Mateus says, youy shouldn\u2019t be removing dice but imposing Difficulty. Storypath avoids altering dice pools as much as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T00:29:19-07:00","id":1449229,"title":"","content":"New version of Reptilians weakness...<br /> <br /> <b>Weakness: Cold Blooded</b> \u2013 As reptiles, Reptilia Sapiens are becoming more and more sluggish as colder it becomes. They get +1 Diffculty to any rolls per 10 degrees below 20 Degrees of Celsius.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T13:14:32-07:00","id":1449279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1447969-reptilians-and-dinosaurs?p=1449229#post1449229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New version of Reptilians weakness...<br /> <br /> <b>Weakness: Cold Blooded</b> \u2013 As reptiles, Reptilia Sapiens are becoming more and more sluggish as colder it becomes. They get +1 Diffculty to any rolls per 10 degrees below 20 Degrees of Celsius.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't want to make the penalty open ended, as anyone could completely shut one down by just making the air super cold. This is bad if they're recurring antagonists, and worse if they're PCs. Try this:<br /> <b>Weakness: Cold Blooded</b> \u2013 As reptiles, Reptilia Sapiens become sluggish as they get colder. They get +1 Difficulty to all rolls per 10 degrees below 20 degrees Celsius, to a maximum of +4 Difficulty.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T22:42:15-07:00","id":1449321,"title":"","content":"Exploring their cold blood may be the best way to deal with an army of reptilians. But they can use heated clothes to avoid it.<br /> <br /> Yet I must agree on the cap. I would go on to a regular cold does +1, very cold +2, Antarctic cold +3 and supernatural cold +4","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom"